 # Geometry and material MLP architecture
 
-Also called: NeuS-style MLP, dual MLP network
+Also called: Geometry Prediction, NeuS-style MLP, SDF and Color Network Prediction, dual MLP network
 
 ## Overview
-This architecture defines the neural network components for decoding signed distance functions (SDF) and material properties (diffuse albedo, specular coefficients) in neural implicit surface reconstruction. It separates geometry and material decoding into two distinct multi-layer perceptrons (MLPs) to improve training stability and rendering fidelity [S1]. It is distinguished from single-MLP approaches by its explicit feature vector passing from the geometry network to the material network, allowing the material decoder to access high-level geometric context [S1].
+This architecture defines the neural network components for decoding signed distance functions (SDF) and material properties (diffuse albedo, specular coefficients) in neural implicit surface reconstruction [S1, S2]. It separates geometry and material decoding into two distinct multi-layer perceptrons (MLPs) [S1]. It is distinguished from single-MLP approaches by its explicit feature vector passing from the geometry network to the material network, allowing the material decoder to access high-level geometric context [S1].
 
 ## How it works
 
 ### Inputs and Outputs
-*   **Geometry MLP Input:** 3D position $\mathbf{x} \in \mathbb{R}^3$ encoded with 6-frequency positional encoding [S1].
-*   **Geometry MLP Output:** Scalar signed distance $d$ and a 256-dimensional feature vector $\mathbf{f} \in \mathbb{R}^{256}$ [S1].
-*   **Material MLP Input:** Concatenation of the 3D position $\mathbf{x}$, the surface normal $\mathbf{n}$, and the feature vector $\mathbf{f}$ from the Geometry MLP [S1].
-*   **Material MLP Output:** 3-channel diffuse albedo $\mathbf{c}_{diff}$ and 27 specular coefficients $\mathbf{c}_{spec}$ [S1].
+*   **Geometry MLP Input:** 3D position $\mathbf{x} \in \mathbb{R}^3$ encoded with 6-frequency positional encoding [S2].
